        "excerpt": "When a Chinese-speaking heir inherits a vacant house in Japan, a real estate agent can do four things right after the death — inspect the site, value it, maintain it, and prepare the sale. You do not have to be in Japan. These can proceed in parallel with the inheritance registration and the division of the estate. A licensed real estate agent and administrative scrivener in Bunkyo, Tokyo sets out the scope from the primary sources.",
