        "excerpt": "The skeleton of a property that can register as a service-provided housing for the elderly (Sakoju) is four things — each unit 25 m² or more in principle (18 m² if the shared areas are ample); a kitchen, toilet, washbasin, bath and storage in each unit or the shared areas; barrier-free corridors, level differences and handrails; and at least a status-check (safety-confirmation) service and a life-consultation service. A licensed real estate agent and administrative scrivener in Bunkyo, Tokyo sets out the property conditions.",
